<title>USA: Value City Department Q4 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Value City Department Q4 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>VALUE CITY DEPARTMENT STORES INC</p>
<p>		    (in millions except per share data)</p>
<p>			  Fourth Quarter Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>				8/03/96  7/29/95  8/03/96     7/29/95</p>
<p>				 13 wks   13 wks   53 wks	52 wks</p>
<p> NET SALES		   $232.5   $211.6 $954.3(a)     $871.9</p>
<p> NET INCOME (LOSS)	    2.1   ( 4.0)     21.7	  13.8</p>
<p>EARNINGS (LOSS) PER</p>
<p>   SHARE			 0.07  ( 0.13)     0.68	  0.43</p>
<p>AVERAGE SHARES</p>
<p>   OUTSTANDING (b)	   31.7     31.9     31.7	  32.0</p>
<p>SHARES USED FOR</p>
<p>   FULLY DILUTED EPS(b)    32.1     32.0     31.9	  32.0</p>
<p>(a) In order to conform to the National Retail Federation's suggested retail calendar, the Company changed its current fiscal year to the Saturday closest to July 31st. This change added one week to the twelve month's results for the current fiscal period.</p>
<p>(b) Excludes 368,600 and 148,900 Treasury Shares at August 3, 1996 and July 29, 1995, respectively.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
